## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_birchbark.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Birch Bark generates a procedural pattern resembling birch tree bark by layering several noise patterns. It can serve as a base for more complex textures.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Birch Bark produit un motif d'écorce de bouleau avec ses lenticelles horizontales et ses fissures verticales, par superposition de bruits.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude and Center set the output range from C-A to C+A; Mask Contrast adjusts contrast before them", "Pattern: Element Size, Element Scale, Offset, Tile Size as repeat interval", "Base Coverage and Base Sharpness: control the cellular base noise", "Lenticels and Lenticel Size: horizontal pore lines", "Cracks and Crack Size: vertical crack lines", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Output can fall below 0 or above 1; use the Clamp options", "Fold has no visible effect when all values are already positive", "Complement assumes values between 0 and 1", "The Contrast post-processing option differs from Noise Contrast on other noise nodes"]

